Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-16-2001||03:25 AM||||I noticed as i was leaving Six Flags today that there's a puddle of fluid that I'm leaving behind. I confirmed it at the Wawa as being mine. It's coming from the right rear of the car, VERY close to the wheel. It's a dark brown fluid, looks like it could be dirty brake fluid or dirty oil. I did hit a big dip the other day and I was airborne for about a second, and came down hard. I'm hoping it wasn' anything najor. I still seem to have the same brake pedal reserve as before, and my oil was pretty clean last time i checked it, which was just a few days before I was flying air fiero. What's the best way for me to diagnose this? TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-16-2001||06:21 AM||||You should be able to identify the fluid by smell and touch. did you check the brake fluid by removing the cover or looking at the fluid level through the plastic. Sometimes a contaminant residue will coat the reservoir sides and give a false indication of the level. It could also be a crank seal, even clean oil would be dirty after weeping outside the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||02:50 PM||||Well there are brake lines in the right rear so that could most defidenly be..stick a piece of white cardboard underthere overnight and diagnois it in the morning..if its oil it should probobly come out faster when the cars running to..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-16-2001||02:55 PM||||Don't know about the color, but when my water pump started leaking, that's where the puddle was piddled. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
